Presidential elections were held in [[Georgia (country)|Georgia]] on 28 October 2018. As no candidate received more than 50% of the vote in the first round, a runoff between [[Salome Zourabichvili]] and [[Grigol Vashadze]] was held on 28 November 2018.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://cesko.ge/eng/list/show/116371-saqartvelos-prezidentis-archevnebis-meore-turi-28-noembers-gaimarteba|title=Second Round of Presidential Election will be Held on November 28|website=Central Election Commission|language=en|access-date=14 November 2018|archive-date=15 November 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181115030803/http://cesko.ge/eng/list/show/116371-saqartvelos-prezidentis-archevnebis-meore-turi-28-noembers-gaimarteba|url-status=dead}}</ref> [[Salome Zourabichvili]] won with around 60% of the vote in the second round<ref name="cec">{{cite web|url=http://results.cec.gov.ge/eng/|title=Results 2018|website=Central Election Commission|access-date=29 November 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171022193854/http://results.cec.gov.ge/eng/|archive-date=22 October 2017|url-status=dead|df=dmy-all}}</ref> and took office on 16 December 2018.

Following amendments to the [[Constitution of Georgia (country)|constitution]] in 2017, the 2018 elections were the last direct presidential vote; subsequential presidential elections were carried out by a 300-member College of Electors. In view of these changes, the President was elected for a term of six years in 2018.<ref name="civil1">{{cite news|title=Key Points of Newly Adopted Constitution|url=http://civil.ge/eng/article.php?id=30474|accessdate=9 December 2017|work=Civil Georgia|date=27 September 2017|language=en}}</ref>

==Background==
The pre-election period was marred by a polarized political environment and a series of secret tape recordings aired by the pro-opposition [[Rustavi 2 TV]], leading to allegations of kidnappings and torture by investigators to secure convictions, pressure and coercion on businesses and media, high-level corruption, and selective justice.<ref>{{cite news|date=17 October 2018|title=Georgia's tapes scandals suggest something is rotten at the top of Georgian politics|work=[[OC Media]]|url=http://oc-media.org/analysis-georgia-s-tapes-scandals-suggest-something-is-rotten-at-the-top-of-georgian-politics/|accessdate=6 January 2019}}</ref>

==Candidates==
46 people applied to participate in the elections, 21 of which were rejected by the [[Election Administration of Georgia]].<ref name=":0" /> 25 presidential candidates were registered by the Election Administration of Georgia.<ref name=":0">{{cite web | url=https://cesko.ge/eng/list/show/114936-2018-tslis-28-oqtombris-archevnebistvis-25-prezidentobis-kandidatia-registrirebuli | title=25 Presidential Candidates are Registered for October 28, 2018 Elections | publisher=Election Administration of Georgia | language=en | date=23 September 2018 | accessdate=20 December 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=http://cesko.ge/res/docs/1.ENG.რეგისტრირებულიკანდიდატები_საიტისთვის.pdf | title=October 28, 2018 Presidential Elections of Georgia Registered Presidential Candidates | publisher=cesko.ge | accessdate=20 December 2020 | archive-date=29 October 2020 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201029185750/https://cesko.ge/res/docs/1.ENG.%E1%83%A0%E1%83%94%E1%83%92%E1%83%98%E1%83%A1%E1%83%A2%E1%83%A0%E1%83%98%E1%83%A0%E1%83%94%E1%83%91%E1%83%A3%E1%83%9A%E1%83%98%E1%83%99%E1%83%90%E1%83%9C%E1%83%93%E1%83%98%E1%83%93%E1%83%90%E1%83%A2%E1%83%94%E1%83%91%E1%83%98_%E1%83%A1%E1%83%90%E1%83%98%E1%83%A2%E1%83%98%E1%83%A1%E1%83%97%E1%83%95%E1%83%98%E1%83%A1.pdf | url-status=dead }}</ref> This is the largest number since Georgia's [[1991 Georgian presidential election|first presidential election in 1991]].<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://civil.ge/archives/255365|title=Presidential Elections 2018: Weekly Digest No. 2|date=25 September 2018|work=Civil.ge|access-date=12 October 2018|language=en-US}}</ref> All 25 candidates were included on the ballot paper.<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://cesko.ge/eng/list/show/115428 |title=The Term for Presidential Candidates to Withdraw their Candidacies has Expired |access-date=16 October 2018 |archive-date=17 October 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181017001739/http://cesko.ge/eng/list/show/115428 |url-status=dead }}</ref>
